## Research summary

**Setup decision.** I compared the passing 5.3.31 test suite against this repo's own history for this exact issue (10 prior automated attempts on branches `ai/kimeta/human-intervention/issue-9399-...`, one of which locally reproduced the 6.0.0 failure with `GVM_TCK_LV=6.0.0 GVM_TCK_NATIVE_IMAGE_MODE=current-defaults`). I independently verified the root cause by pulling `spring-aspects-6.0.0-sources.jar`: `org.springframework.context.annotation.aspectj.SpringConfiguredConfiguration`, `org.springframework.transaction.aspectj.AspectJTransactionManagementConfiguration`, `org.springframework.scheduling.aspectj.AspectJAsyncConfiguration`, and `org.springframework.cache.aspectj.AspectJCachingConfiguration` are all plain `@Configuration` classes (no `proxyBeanMethods = false`), i.e. "full mode." When the existing test's `@EnableSpringConfigured` / `@Enable*(mode = AdviceMode.ASPECTJ)` tests boot a real `AnnotationConfigApplicationContext`, Spring's `ConfigurationClassPostProcessor` CGLIB-enhances these library-internal classes at runtime and also ASM-parses selector classes (e.g. `AsyncConfigurationSelector.class`) as classpath resources — both traced in a prior local run's stack traces (`BeanDefinitionStoreException` → `FileNotFoundException: .../AsyncConfigurationSelector.class`, and the earlier verified `UnsupportedFeatureError` from CGLIB `ReflectUtils.defineClass`). No Maven dependency, Docker image, or env/system-property fix addresses this — it requires writing the test differently, so this is `agent_guidance`, not `deterministic_setup`.

**Unsupportable check.** The issue body's own failure log is truncated before the actual exception, so step 1 (FAILURE from the issue's evidence alone) can't be completed — that alone rules out `skip_unsupported`. Separately, even using the traced mechanism: a viable fallback exists (the existing 5.3.31 suite already exercises `AnnotationBeanConfigurerAspect`, `AnnotationTransactionAspect`, `AnnotationCacheAspect`, and `AnnotationAsyncExecutionAspect` via their static `aspectOf()` accessors instead of booting a full context), so SOLE PATH fails — this is repairable, not unsupportable.

